  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: LolaBebang_W81_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Lola Bebang
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Ket ita, nakadanonka iti sabali pay a napateg a saludsod.


    No
    kayatmo a damagen ti bilang wenno kadakkel ti maysa a grupo, agusar ti Ilokano
    iti ''mano'' para iti ''how many.''


    Mabalinmo nga agusar iti daytoy no
    damagem ti bilang dagiti tattao wenno banag.


    Denggem a naimbag: mano.


    Ita,
    padasem nga ibagam ti ''mano'' iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'And now, you''ve reached another important question.

    When
    you want to ask about quantity, Ilokano uses ''mano'' for ''how many.''

    You
    can use it when asking about the number of people or objects.

    Now, try saying
    ''mano'' yourself.'
